course: dictionary
lesson: 9277
title: One word, more than one meaning
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the context tells you which one is meant. The word spam has three. Read the words around it and ask which meaning fits. «A spam filter can give points to warning words and flag a message» is about messages on a computer, so here spam means unwanted messages.
explain: Spam can also be a verb. «To spam» means to send lots of unwanted messages, or to post the same thing again and again. Check your meaning by putting it into the sentence. Does it still make sense?
explain: «Spam is also a brand of tinned meat» is a clue too. A brand is a company's name for its products, so this spam is a food. When one word has several meanings, read on for the clue words.
fact: Spam (noun) means unwanted messages sent to many people at once, usually emails or texts.
fact: Spam (verb) means to send lots of unwanted messages, or to post the same thing again and again.
fact: Spam can also mean a brand of tinned cooked pork meat, made in the USA and famous in wartime Britain.
fact: The junk-message meaning comes from a 1970 Monty Python comedy sketch, where people sing «Spam» over and over until everything else is drowned out.
fact: Never click on, reply to, or trust a spam message. Report it or delete it, and check your spam or junk folder for real emails.
exercise: «A spam filter can give points to warning words and flag a message.» What does spam mean here? | A sticky sauce for pasta | *Unwanted junk messages | Tinned cooked pork meat | A fast, angry email
exercise: «Spam filters use AI to spot junk and scam emails, but some real emails end up in the spam folder too.» What does spam folder mean? | A folder for family photos | A folder for birthday cards | A folder for tinned food | *A folder for unwanted junk messages
exercise: «Spam is also a brand of tinned meat.» Which meaning of spam is this? | *A food made from cooked pork | To send the same message again and again | Unwanted messages sent to many people | A type of computer game
test: «He spammed the chat with the same message ten times.» Which meaning of spam is this? | Tinned cooked pork meat | A spam filter that catches junk | Unwanted junk messages in an inbox | *To send lots of unwanted messages again and again
test: Which sentence uses spam as a verb? | The spam folder was full of old emails. | *He spammed the chat with the same message ten times. | We ate a Spam sandwich for lunch. | The spam filter flagged the email as junk.
exam: «We opened a tin of Spam for lunch.» Which meaning fits best? | To send the same message again and again | A scam email asking for your password | Unwanted junk messages sent to many people | *Tinned cooked pork meat
